<title>MEXICO: Carso completes Sears de Mexico buy.</title>
<headline>Carso completes Sears de Mexico buy.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican conglomerate Grupo Carso SA said on Monday it had completed the purchase of 60 percent of Sears Roebuck de Mexico SA for $103 million or $2.2889 per share.</p>
<p>Sears Roebuck and Co. kept a 15 percent stake in its Mexican unit. Carso will own the remaining shares at a price of 18.1096 pesos per share once legal authorization has been obtained, Carso said in a statement.</p>
<p>Carso, Mexico's largest conglomerate, announced it would buy Sears' troubled Mexican operations on April 2.</p>
<p>(--David Luhnow, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
